            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">How do I register our startup/small business deployment?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-base text-gray-600">
              You can register your deployment using our <a href="/register/" target="_blank" class="text-brand-600 font-semibold hover:underline">business registration form</a>. Registration is a licensing requirement for commercial use, and it ensures you receive critical security patches and product updates.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="py-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">What is the difference between Community and Enterprise?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-base text-gray-600">
              The Community Version includes all core metrics, logs, and alerting capabilities to monitor your infrastructure locally. The Enterprise Version adds hybrid cloud features, automated system upgrades, SMS and voice notification channels, and priority SLAs.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="py-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Where does our monitoring data reside?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-base text-gray-600">
              Your data stays completely under your control on your own infrastructure. ZoomPhant uses open, standard formats (Prometheus-compatible for metrics and Loki-compatible for logs) so you never experience vendor lock-in.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="py-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">What's the difference between ZoomPhant and ZoomPhant TSDB?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-base text-gray-600">
              <strong>ZoomPhant</strong> is our enterprise-grade, production-ready monitoring platform with full dashboards, visual collector management, high performance at scale, and comprehensive UI. It's designed for teams running serious production workloads and needing a complete observability solution.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base text-gray-600">
              <strong>ZoomPhant TSDB</strong> is a developer-first, lightweight time-series database for <strong>development, testing, and small-scale use cases</strong>. It's agent-first (push from code/CI/CD), API-first (headless with minimal UI), stores metrics + logs together, and uses a two-tier label system to prevent cardinality issues. TSDB runs on Cloudflare's edge (free tier or ~$5/month) but is <strong>not designed for enterprise production monitoring</strong>—for that, use ZoomPhant platform.
